# OpenSpec Guardian Mode

Follow `docs/ai/rules/openspec-guardian.md`. It owns the triggers, the context packet for `/openspec-guardian`, the completion gate and the prompt template.

- `/openspec-guardian` (`.cursor/agents/openspec-guardian.md`) checks direction, scope, prompt intent and OpenSpec alignment. `/qa-foreman` checks quality, tests, edge cases and completion. For careful implementation, use both.
- Read `AGENTS.md`, `openspec/project.md`, `docs/ai/rules/openspec.md`, the relevant `openspec/specs/**` and any active `openspec/changes/**` before coding.
- The Guardian is permanently read-only: no file writes, no shell mutation, no OpenSpec sync or archive.
- Distinguish intended behavior from current reality. Active changes do not prove shipped behavior.
- Asym Postgres owns all CRM truth. Twenty CRM is retired. Escalate material source conflicts.
- If the verdict is `NEEDS_OPENSPEC_CHANGE`, stop broad implementation until the change is created or updated. Do not rewrite OpenSpec to justify drifted code.
